      "subtitle": "Series 3: Episode 1",
      "synopses": {
       "large": "As we continue to expand our urban spaces and cities, our wildlife has felt the consequences.\n\nWildlife film-maker Libby Penman showcases the incredible work of dedicated conservationists who are fighting to bring our wildlife back from the brink. As we journey across Europe, we see how bottlenose dolphins are thriving in Aberdeen Harbour, how pioneering designers in Munich are reimagining urban construction with wildlife at its heart, and we meet the Ibizan scientific community that is rallying towns together to save an iconic lizard species.\n\nWe see teams in Scotland that are working to protect peregrine falcons from poachers and the citizen science project in Ireland that is researching how red foxes are adapting to our city life, and dive with a dedicated woman creating change in the waterways of the Netherlands.\n\nAcross all of these stories, Libby reveals the benefits of supporting and living alongside our wildlife. The amazing work of these groups and individuals show that if we take care of nature, it will take care of us in return.",
       "small": "Libby Penman showcases incredible nature conservation success stories from across Europe.",
       "medium": "From dolphins in Scotland to bats in Slovenia, Libby Penman showcases European nature stories that celebrate the incredible work of people fighting to save Europe's wildlife.",
       "editorial": "Good news for nature. Stories of hope, wildlife and new thinking from across Europe"
      },
